{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 488 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b6b0689bcfac999d4bee823e3d39e28d1afdeaeb4969a31aac893b43d710b6e2" :edb/db-before-t 487 :edb/db-after-t 488 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533800 50 #inst "2026-10-05T01:19:07.865Z" 13194139533800 true] [17592186110645 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252087 13194139533800 true] [17592186110645 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252094 13194139533800 true] [17592186110645 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252121 13194139533800 true] [17592186110646 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252084 13194139533800 true] [17592186110646 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252101 13194139533800 true] [17592186110646 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252108 13194139533800 true] [17592186110647 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252115 13194139533800 true] [17592186110647 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252118 13194139533800 true] [17592186110647 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252128 13194139533800 true] [17592186110647 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252135 13194139533800 true] [17592186110647 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252142 13194139533800 true] [17592186111060 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186111060 1145 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =x+1 \\\\ 2x-x & =x+1-x \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x=x+1$ has the unique solution $x=1.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =2x+1 \\\\ 2x+1-2x & =2x+1-2x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x+1=2x+1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =2x+3 \\\\ 2x+1-2x & =2x+3-2x \\\\ 1 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533800 true] [17592186111061 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186111061 1145 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n2p=3.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533800 true] [17592186111062 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186111062 1145 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=p-3,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\np-3=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=7.\n$$" 13194139533800 true] [17592186111065 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186111065 1145 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =2x+5 \\\\ 3x-2x & =2x+5-2x \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3x=2x+5$ has the unique solution $x=5.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =4x-2 \\\\ 4x-2-4x & =4x-2-4x \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x-2=4x-2$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3 & =5x+1 \\\\ 5x+3-5x & =5x+1-5x \\\\ 3 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252085 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1089 "q-287975" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1100 "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(2p-3)x=5x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1113 #uuid "ceb241e1-ab0e-5069-a882-fcb4fcc9530e" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252084 1145 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p-3,\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n2p-3=5.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p & =8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252085 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252086 13194139533800 true] [17592186252085 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533800 true] [17592186252085 1041 "field-1" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252085 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252086 13194139533800 true] [17592186252085 1110 #uuid "ae1df2cf-9566-5004-8ba6-32d65599da18" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252086 1034 "4" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533800 true] [17592186252086 1111 #uuid "9c63cda8-2840-56f2-8271-c21f55da3cae" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252088 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1089 "q-288425" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1100 "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\n- $-3x+2=-3x+7$\n- $6x+1=6x+5$\n- $7x-4=6x-6$" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1113 #uuid "e7142601-1b63-5b13-9c8c-802df3891cac" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252087 1145 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2 & =-3x+7 \\\\ -3x+2+3x & =-3x+7+3x \\\\ 2 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+5 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+5-6x \\\\ 1 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-4 & =6x-6 \\\\ 7x-4-6x & =6x-6-6x \\\\ x-4 & =-6 \\\\ x-4+4 & =-6+4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $7x-4=6x-6$ has the unique solution $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252089 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252090 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252091 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252092 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252093 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1041 "selection" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252091 13194139533800 true] [17592186252088 1110 #uuid "564067cd-fa2c-5738-b6b8-fba47708cbc1" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252089 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252089 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252089 1111 #uuid "3cb7c1e6-18fb-5883-8ac3-e8038cf665d4" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252090 1034 "III only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252090 1111 #uuid "135c8097-040c-5eaa-bd48-8c1bd1be1ce1" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252091 1034 "None" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252091 1111 #uuid "57cfaaeb-39d3-5e02-8d43-1b5d2094213d" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252092 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252092 1111 #uuid "2a307c03-89b0-56b3-b26c-60c731cd0cda" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252093 1034 "II only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252093 1111 #uuid "0041155f-65d3-516a-bbc3-ce5282877436" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252095 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1089 "q-288427" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1100 "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\n- $2x-5=x-2$\n- $6x+1=6x+9$\n- $-4x+3=-4x+3$" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1113 #uuid "4aab251b-8c37-5d06-8cf8-88c1adaf045f" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252094 1145 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & =x-2 \\\\ 2x-5-x & =x-2-x \\\\ x-5 & =-2 \\\\ x-5+5 & =-2+5 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x-5=x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+9 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+9-6x \\\\ 1 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3 & =-4x+3 \\\\ -4x+3+4x & =-4x+3+4x \\\\ 3 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-4x+3=-4x+3$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252096 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252097 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252098 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252099 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252100 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1041 "selection" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252098 13194139533800 true] [17592186252095 1110 #uuid "6d9ab049-7072-55db-a7a3-b956c894bb34" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252096 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533800 true] [17592186252096 1111 #uuid "5702e069-3db0-5b29-b6ad-3fe304c18fa5" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252097 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533800 true] [17592186252097 1103